      "timestamp": "2026-09-26T07:02:33.281Z",
      "message": "The change itself is one line — `SESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30` → `480` in `config.js:3` (`server.js:3` is the only consumer, and it just reads the value, so nothing else needs touching).\n\nBefore I make it, the consequence: this is a session lifetime, so it's a security-posture change, not just a constant. Going from 30 minutes to 8 hours means a stolen or hijacked session token stays valid for a full working day, and an unattended logged-in browser stays authenticated all day rather than self-expiring over a lunch break. That's a 16x widening of the window for session hijacking. Whether that's acceptable depends on what this app holds and whether there's any idle-timeout or re-auth layer separate from this value — there isn't one in this repo.\n\nConfirm and I'll make the change as asked. If you want something in between, the common middle ground is a long absolute cap (8h) paired with a shorter idle timeout (~30m), but that's a second mechanism this codebase doesn't currently have.",
      "model_name": "claude-opus-5"
